<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 20.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 20.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period February 18-20.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Feb 18 (actual) 312 mcm, 73 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 19 (forecast) 322 mcm, 75 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 20 (forecast) 316 cm, 74 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Feb 18 (actual) 4.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.5 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 19 (forecast) 7.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.6 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 20 (forecast) 7.7 Celsius, seasonal normal  4.6 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on the system on Wednesday, and TransCo says the probability of interruption on Thursday is &quot;low&quot; in every Local Distribution Zone.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
